  members: ModuleDoc ModuleDocComment 0..96 "//! `impl I for T { members }` writes the witness of an interface for a type: the target names a"
  members: ModuleDoc ModuleDocComment 97..195 "//! type, or a type constructor and the parameters it binds with `$` (spec 02, section 3). Without"
  members: ModuleDoc ModuleDocComment 196..291 "//! `I for` it adds methods to the type, and with `= value` the witness is the value. What each"
  members: ModuleDoc ModuleDocComment 292..389 "//! stands for is `#[impl(I(T))]` on a declaration, so it conforms, registers and is found alike."
